  "introduction": {
    "title": "Where Curiosity Became a Career",
    "description": [
      "I didn't begin my career writing software. I began by asking questions.",
      "I've always been fascinated by how complex systems work—how individual components interact, communicate, and come together to solve meaningful problems.",
      "My academic background in Mechanical Engineering taught me to think in systems: understanding constraints, analyzing relationships, and designing solutions that are reliable and efficient.",
      "As I discovered software engineering, I realized those same principles existed in the digital world. Software wasn't simply writing code—it was designing systems, creating abstractions, and solving problems through logic.",
      "The ability to transform ideas into working products with nothing more than a computer sparked a new passion.",
      "What started as curiosity gradually became a commitment to mastering software engineering and building products that people genuinely enjoy using."
    ],
    "modules": [
      "HTML",
      "CSS",
      "JavaScript",
      "React",
      "Computer Science Fundamentals"
    ]
  },

  "learningJourney": {
    "title": "Learning Through Building",
    "description": [
      "My programming journey began with The Odin Project, a curriculum built around a simple philosophy: the best way to learn is by building real software.",
      "Rather than memorizing syntax, every project introduced a new engineering concept that built upon the previous one.",
      "I learned to understand not only how to write code, but why programming languages, frameworks, and design patterns exist.",
      "Throughout the journey I explored:",
      [
        "How browsers render web pages",
        "Semantic HTML and accessibility",
        "Modern CSS layouts",
        "JavaScript fundamentals",
        "DOM manipulation",
        "Algorithms and computational thinking",
        "Object-Oriented Programming",
        "Functional Programming",
        "Closures and scope",
        "Software design patterns",
        "REST APIs",
        "React component architecture"
      ],
      "Every project became an opportunity to explore a new engineering concept.",
      "Every bug became a debugging exercise.",
      "Every refactor improved not only the codebase, but also the way I approached solving problems.",
      "By the end of this journey, I had moved beyond learning syntax and started thinking like a software engineer."
    ]
  },

